  <h2>Household safety</h2>
  <p>A direct statement such as “Sam is allergic to peanuts” is saved immediately and acknowledged. “Sam dislikes peanuts” remains an ordinary preference. If “we avoid peanuts” could mean a preference, household rule or allergy, Chef asks before putting it in the safety section.</p>
  <p>Meal feedback can become an observation or preference, but it never silently becomes an allergy. Removing or weakening an existing safety requirement needs an explicit instruction. A meal that appeared safe does not weaken anything, and Chef is not medical advice.</p>

  <h2>From list to basket</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>“Make my grocery list” creates or updates a list. It does not touch a retailer basket.</li>
    <li>“Fill my cart” is sufficient authority to prepare that basket. Chef does not demand an approval token or repeated phrase.</li>
    <li>Chef inspects and preserves existing items before making changes.</li>
    <li>It resolves sensible purchase quantities and checks explicit dietary requirements against visible product information where possible.</li>
    <li>It inspects the final basket and names anything it could not verify.</li>
    <li>The user takes over before checkout, fulfilment or payment.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Computer Use beta</h2>
  <p>Chef first checks whether the user's agent has an appropriate browser, Computer Use or shopping capability. If it does not, Chef provides the grocery list and says the basket was not changed. The user remains responsible for each provider's terms.</p>
  <p>Clicks are not proof. Chef re-opens or refreshes the basket, compares intended final quantities and reports any unavailable or unverified line plainly. Verified additions can remain in place even when another line is incomplete, but Chef must not call the whole basket ready.</p>

  <h2>Hard stop</h2>
  <p>Chef does not perform checkout, payment, delivery or pickup confirmation, address changes, subscription enrolment, restricted-product decisions or order placement. It does not bundle a named retailer adapter and does not bypass access controls or bot protections.</p>
</ChefPageLayout>
